  "note": "Election of the Cookstown Urban District Council, polled Friday 15 January 1926; four members returned unopposed (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1926, p. 10). 'C00KST0WN. Nominations for four vacancies:—Messrs Hugh Elliott, Thomas Gibson (chairman), Joseph F. Thompson (retiring councillors), and Mr. George Faulkner in the place of James Bell, now left the district.' Four nominations for four vacancies, so no poll. No party label printed. Returned unopposed."
